  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Methylatropine is a semisynthetic quaternary belladonna alkaloid with parasympatholytic (anticholinergic) activity, classed for drugs used against functional gastrointestinal disorders. It appears to be only an experimental compound today, with no authorised marketing recorded in the European Union, so its current clinical use is unclear.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27269116&quot;>Wikidata Q27269116</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>methylatropine</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>A03BB02</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB13833&quot;>DB13833</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/656598&quot;>656598</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q27269116&quot;>Q27269116</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C18H26NO3+</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>304.41 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
